! version = 2.0

// "about wilson" deliberately not repeated here — cv.rive's summary
// trigger already lists it verbatim, and an identical bare-alternation
// item in two different files is a silent tie the sort order happens to
// resolve in cv.rive's favor (confirmed by testing), which would only
// get more fragile as more triggers are added. cv.rive owns that phrase.
+ (cv|resume|about my cv|wilson cv)
- Sure, let's talk about Wilson's CV. Ask about his summary, skills, languages, education, or experience.

// Open-ended "tell me more about Wilson" style phrasing — distinct from
// the exact-match trigger above (whose reply is a different, narrower
// CTA); wrapped with [*] since the trigger above is alternation-only and
// won't match as a substring of a longer sentence. Still loses to that
// exact trigger for the bare short forms ("about wilson", "tell me about
// wilson" with nothing else) since RiveScript prefers the more specific,
// wildcard-free match — confirmed by testing. That's fine: this trigger
// exists for the longer, natural-sentence phrasings, not the bare forms.
+ [*] (want to know more about wilson|want to know about wilson|know more about wilson|learn more about wilson|tell me more about wilson|tell me about wilson) [*]
- {@ setintent wilsonoverview}{@ ctrlintent wilsonoverview}<set pendingtopic=experience>What would you like to know about Wilson? We can start with his experience, what do you think?
- {@ setintent wilsonoverview}{@ ctrlintent wilsonoverview}<set pendingtopic=skills>What would you like to know about Wilson? We can start with his skills, what do you think?
- {@ setintent wilsonoverview}{@ ctrlintent wilsonoverview}<set pendingtopic=education>What would you like to know about Wilson? We can start with his education, what do you think?
- {@ setintent wilsonoverview}{@ ctrlintent wilsonoverview}<set pendingtopic=languages>What would you like to know about Wilson? We can start with the languages he speaks, what do you think?

+ (@yeswords) [*]
% [*] what do you think [*]
* <get pendingtopic> == skills => {@ what are your skills}
* <get pendingtopic> == education => {@ what is your education}
* <get pendingtopic> == languages => {@ what languages do you speak}
- {@ what is your experience}

+ (@nowords) [*]
% [*] what do you think [*]
- <set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=wilsonoverviewfollowup><set botIntention=<bot intent_wilsonoverviewfollowup>>No problem! You can ask about Wilson's skills, education, languages, or a specific company instead.

+ (@maybewords) [*]
% [*] what do you think [*]
- <set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=wilsonoverviewfollowup><set botIntention=<bot intent_wilsonoverviewfollowup>>No worries — I am here whenever you are ready. Just ask about anything related to Wilson, like his skills, experience, or education.

// Generic "what else can you tell me" continuation prompt — previously
// fell straight through to unknown.rive's catch-all instead of
// continuing whatever topic was already in play (reported bug: asked
// about skills, then "what else can you tell me?" got a generic "I did
// not quite follow" reply instead of more detail or a topic suggestion).
// Branches on the CURRENT userIntention and reuses the exact same
// follow-up flows already established for the experience and
// company-blurb replies (experiencefollowup/companyfollowup — see
// cv.rive's %-scoped yeswords blocks for the original versions of these
// two messages) rather than inventing new topic-suggestion text.
// followupgroup_<key> (begin.rive) groups the five company intents so
// one condition covers all of them instead of five separate `==` checks
// — same dynamic bot-var-by-key lookup already used for intent_<key>.
//
// [*] on both sides since these are natural-sentence phrasings, not
// exact short forms (same convention as "tell me more about wilson"
// above). Deliberately does NOT include bare "tell me more": that
// phrase is a *substring* of "tell me more about wilson" (claimed by
// the trigger above) and of cv.rive's atomic "tell me more" ->
// career-summary trigger, and both this trigger and the one above are
// in the same word-count/wildcard sort bucket, where RiveScript ties by
// raw pattern length rather than semantic specificity — including it
// here made this trigger win that tie and swallow "tell me more about
// wilson", breaking the wilsonoverview flow (confirmed by testing: it
// regressed the existing "yes after the randomized prompt" test). The
// other phrasings below don't share a substring with either of those,
// so they're safe.
+ [*] (what else can you tell me|what else|anything else|tell me something else|what other things can you tell me|what more can you tell me|anything more) [*]
* <get currentSession> == opening => <set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=genericfollowup><set botIntention=<bot intent_genericfollowup>>Not sure what you would like more detail on yet — you can ask about Wilson's summary, skills, languages, education, experience, or a specific company.
* <get userIntention> == experience => <set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=experiencefollowup><set botIntention=<bot intent_experiencefollowup>>Sure — his most recent role has been at Smart Debrief. Ask about that, or any other company, skill, or topic you are curious about.
* <bot followupgroup_<get userIntention>> == company => <set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=companyfollowup><set botIntention=<bot intent_companyfollowup>>Sure! You can ask about Smart Debrief, Moomenti, Mobiweb, Red IT, or Exact Code Sistemas, or about a specific skill like frontend, mobile, testing, or AI.
- That is everything specific I have on <bot intent_<get userIntention>> for now. You can also ask about Wilson's summary, skills, languages, education, experience, or a specific company like Smart Debrief or Moomenti.<set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=genericfollowup><set botIntention=<bot intent_genericfollowup>>

+ [lets] (chat|small talk|conversation|talk to me)
- Sure, let's chat. Ask me anything, or say "joke" for a laugh.

+ (reset|start over|go home|home)
- Resetting our conversation. {topic=random}
